description:
Monitor one or more Jules sessions with optional waiting until terminal or action-required state. Sessions that cannot be polled at all (e.g. unknown IDs) are reported in the errored bucket while the rest keep polling.

Use this for consolidated status checks, or set wait=true after dispatching when an AI agent needs completed/failed/cancelled/action-required/errored/still-running buckets before the next orchestration step.

Returns without wait: { success: true, data: { sessions: [{ sessionId, title, state, status, prUrl?, lastActivity? }] } }

Returns with wait: { success: true, data: { sessions, wait: { completed, failed, cancelled, awaitingPlan, awaitingUserFeedback, paused, actionRequired, errored, errors: [{ sessionId, message }], stillRunning, timedOut } } }

See also: jules_dispatch (create sessions), jules_interact (inspect one session in full context), jules_list_sessions (discover recent IDs)
